marked 18.1.3, vendored as this repository's renderer and MODIFIED:
marked.esm.js below carries literal-character guards spliced into its two tokenizer loops
(12 edits in the inline loop, one of them a helper function, 11 edits in the block loop, and
12 further edits that cut per-token whole-document work and regexes that cannot match;
35 edits in all). Each guard tests the first character the corresponding anchored tokenizer
rule must start with, so it is a necessary condition and the HTML cannot change; the further
edits are equally exact (a cheaper way to take the first line, a skipped no-op replace, a
tighter necessary condition). All 720 practice cases are byte-identical to unmodified
marked's output, and 20000 differentially fuzzed inputs diverge in 0 cases. The edits, with
before/after text and rationale, are in README.md at the repository root.

